.env
.env.*
# `deploy/community/openppwr.env` is the file the deployment documentation tells every operator to create,
# and it holds the database, worker and bootstrap credentials of a live stack. It is not `.env` and does not
# start with `.env`, so neither rule above covered it: `git check-ignore` returned "not ignored". Its
# directory is publicly exported, so a single `git add -A` on a deployment host would have committed live
# secrets into the release. Ignore any name ending in `.env`, not only the dotfile forms.
*.env
!.env.example
!*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.crt
*.cer
*.dump
*.backup
*.bak
*.log
apps/web/public/downloads/
artifacts/reporting/
